---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = '1 November 2026';
const toc = [
  { id: 'agreement', label: 'Agreement to these terms' },
  { id: 'who-we-are', label: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'what-this-site-is', label: 'What this site is, and is not' },
  { id: 'product-information', label: 'Product information' },
  { id: 'oe-references', label: 'OE references and part numbers' },
  { id: 'quotations-orders', label: 'Quotations and orders' },
  { id: 'prices', label: 'Prices, taxes and delivery' },
  { id: 'acceptable-use', label: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'intellectual-property', label: 'Intellectual property' },
  { id: 'third-party', label: 'Third-party links' },
  { id: 'warranties', label: 'Disclaimer of warranties' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Limitation of liability' },
  { id: 'indemnity', label: 'Indemnity' },
  { id: 'governing-law', label: 'Governing law and disputes' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes and severability' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms governing use of China Filter Hub: data status, quotations and orders, acceptable use, intellectual property and liability."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Terms of Service', href: '/terms/' }]}
  updated="2026-11-01"
>
  <LegalPage
    title="Terms of Service"
    updated={updated}
    toc={toc}
    intro="These terms govern your use of chinafilterhub.com and data.chinafilterhub.com. They set out what this site is — an information and cross-reference resource — what it is not, and the basis on which information on it is provided."
  >
    <h2 id="agreement">1. Agreement to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      By accessing this website you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please stop using
      the site. If you use the site on behalf of a company, you confirm that you are authorised to
      accept these terms for that company, and &ldquo;you&rdquo; includes the company.
    </p>
    <p>
      These terms apply to the website. They do not replace the terms of any individual contract of
      sale, quotation, or supply agreement, which prevail over these terms in the event of a
      conflict.
    </p>

    <h2 id="who-we-are">2. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This website is operated by <strong>{site.entity.legalName}</strong>, a company registered in
      Qinghe County, Hebei, China, under unified social credit code
      <code>{site.entity.creditCode}</code>, with its registered address at {site.entity.address}.
      Contact details are set out in section 16.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what-this-site-is">3. What this site is, and what it is not</h2>
    <p>
      China Filter Hub is a product information and cross-reference resource for automotive, HVAC,
      cleanroom and industrial filtration products. It exists to help buyers identify a part, read
      its recorded specification, and decide whether to request a quotation.
    </p>
    <p><strong>The site is not:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>an online shop — no order is placed or accepted by using the site;</li>
      <li>a marketplace — we do not host third-party sellers or process payments;</li>
      <li>a certification body — we do not certify that any product meets a standard;</li>
      <li>a substitute for the original equipment manufacturer&rsquo;s documentation.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="product-information">4. Product information and specifications</h2>
    <p>
      Specifications on this site are compiled from manufacturer catalogues, published standards,
      and supplier documentation. Each field carries a data-status label indicating how it was
      obtained. Where a value could not be verified from a traceable source, the field is left
      blank rather than estimated.
    </p>
    <p>
      Dimensions, media, efficiency ratings and interchange information can change between
      production batches and model years, and catalogues are occasionally wrong. Information on
      this site is therefore <strong>indicative</strong>. Before you place an order, confirm the
      specification against the OE drawing, the vehicle or equipment identification, or a physical
      sample. Section 11 explains the limits of what we warrant.
    </p>

    <h2 id="oe-references">5. OE references and part numbers</h2>
    <p>
      OE numbers and competitor part numbers are reproduced for identification purposes only. A
      cross-reference on this site means that a part has been recorded as associated with that
      number — it does <strong>not</strong> by itself confirm dimensional equivalence, material
      equivalence, or fitness for a particular application.
    </p>
    <p>
      Manufacturer names and trademarks are the property of their respective owners and are used
      descriptively, to identify the application a part is intended for. Their use does not imply
      any affiliation with, endorsement by, or approval of us by those manufacturers.
    </p>

    <h2 id="quotations-orders">6. Quotations and orders</h2>
    <p>
      Submitting a request for quotation through this site is an invitation to us to quote. It does
      not create a contract, reserve stock, or fix a price. A quotation is valid for the period
      stated in it, or for 30 days if no period is stated, and is subject to the availability of
      materials at the time of acceptance.
    </p>
    <p>
      A contract of sale is formed only when we issue a written order confirmation or proforma
      invoice and you accept it. Any samples, drawings or pre-production approvals are governed by
      the terms stated in that confirmation.
    </p>

    <h2 id="prices">7. Prices, taxes and delivery</h2>
    <p>
      Prices quoted through this site are in the currency stated on the quotation and are exclusive
      of taxes, duties and freight unless stated otherwise. International Commercial Terms
      (Incoterms) are specified per quotation; where they are not, they are agreed in writing
      before shipment. Import duties, value-added tax and customs clearance in the destination
      country are the buyer&rsquo;s responsibility unless the quotation expressly states otherwise.
    </p>
    <p>
      Lead times are estimates based on production capacity at the time of quotation and are not
      guaranteed unless expressly agreed as a contractual delivery date.
    </p>

    <h2 id="acceptable-use">8. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>use the site in breach of any applicable law or regulation;</li>
      <li>attempt to gain unauthorised access to the site, its servers, or any connected system;</li>
      <li>introduce malware, or interfere with the availability or integrity of the site;</li>
      <li>extract data at a rate or in a manner that imposes an unreasonable load, or that circumvents rate limits and access controls;</li>
      <li>reproduce the database or a substantial part of it for a competing service;</li>
      <li>misrepresent your identity, your company, or your authority to act for a company; or</li>
      <li>use contact details published on this site to send unsolicited bulk messages.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Automated access for search indexing is permitted subject to our robots directives. Other
      automated collection requires our prior written consent.
    </p>

    <h2 id="intellectual-property">9. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The layout, text, original descriptions, data compilation and design of this site are owned by
      us or used under licence, and are protected by copyright and database rights. You may view,
      download and print pages for your own internal business evaluation. You may not republish,
      resell, or create a derivative database from them without written permission.
    </p>
    <p>
      Third-party trademarks, part numbers and catalogue references remain the property of their
      owners. Nothing in these terms grants you a licence to use any third-party mark.
    </p>

    <h2 id="third-party">10. Third-party links and content</h2>
    <p>
      The site links to external resources, including messaging services and public reference
      sources. Those sites are not under our control, and we are not responsible for their content,
      accuracy or practices. A link is not an endorsement.
    </p>

    <h2 id="warranties">11. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
    <p>
      The site and its content are provided on an &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as
      available&rdquo; basis. To the fullest extent permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties,
      express or implied, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
      purpose, and non-infringement.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not warrant that the site will be uninterrupted, error-free or free of harmful
      components, or that any specification, cross-reference or other content is accurate, complete
      or current. Warranties for goods supplied under a contract of sale are set out in that
      contract and are not affected by this section.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">12. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special,
      consequential or punitive loss, or for loss of profit, revenue, business, goodwill, data, or
      anticipated savings, arising from your use of or inability to use this site, or from reliance
      on its content.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our aggregate liability arising out of or in connection with your use of the site is limited
      to the amount you paid us, if any, for the product or service giving rise to the claim.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or
      limited, including liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or
      for any other liability that applicable law does not permit to be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2 id="indemnity">13. Indemnity</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to indemnify us against claims, losses and reasonable costs arising from your breach
      of these terms, your misuse of the site, or your infringement of the rights of a third party.
      This does not apply to the extent the claim arises from our own negligence or breach.
    </p>

    <h2 id="governing-law">14. Governing law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the People&rsquo;s Republic of China, without regard
      to conflict-of-law rules. The parties will first attempt to resolve any dispute through good-
      faith negotiation. If it is not resolved within 30 days, either party may bring proceedings in
      the people&rsquo;s court with jurisdiction at the defendant&rsquo;s domicile.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing in this section deprives a consumer of the protection of mandatory rules of the law of
      their country of residence, where those rules apply.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">15. Changes and severability</h2>
    <p>
      We may revise these terms from time to time. The version published on this page, with the
      date shown above, is the current version and applies from the date of publication. If any
      provision is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue in full force, and the
      unenforceable provision is replaced by the closest enforceable equivalent.
    </p>
    <p>
      These terms, together with the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>,
      <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> and <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>, constitute
      the entire agreement between us regarding use of the site.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">16. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {site.entity.legalName}<br />
      {site.entity.address}<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.entity.email}`}>{site.entity.email}</a> ·{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.entity.emailAlt}`}>{site.entity.emailAlt}</a><br />
      Telephone / WhatsApp: {site.entity.phone}
    </p>
    <p class="muted small">
      See also: <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> · <a href="/company/">Company details</a>
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
